	   ***  tAo v3.3 PARAMETERS FILE  ***
	        (default unities : I.S.)


Comments on this project: --


PARAMETER  CORRESPONDING 		
 VALUES     VARIABLES			USE
-------	----------------------	--------------------------------------------

Gridding:
401 	Nx			Number of x points (distance axis).
201	Nz			Number of z points (depth axis for elastic-plastic model).

Limits of x domain:
0	x0			Left
4e5	xf			Right

Limits of the output window:
000e3	xmin			Left
150e3	xmax			Right
-2000	ymin			Bottom
500	ymax			Top


Lithosph. geometry:
10000	Te_default		Default Elastic Thickness (if no .EET file). Te=0 => local isostasy.
32000	crust_thick_default 	Default crustal geometry for gravity anomaly and rheological calculations when no .CRUST and .UCRUST
15000	upper_crust_thick_default 	Id. for upper crust.
0	alt0 			Altitude of the initial plate position from sea level.


Densities:
3300	densmantle		Mantle density.
2850	denscrust		Crust (just for anomaly calculation).
2800	densinfill		Infilling material (only when switch_topoest=1).
2300	denssedim		Sediments.
000	densamb			Air (or water for oceanic flexure).


Erosion model parameters (used only if switch_erosed=1):
0e6	Kerosdif 		Diffusive erosion constant [m2/Ma].
1	Keroseol 		Continental background erosion rate constant meters of sediment by meters of height and My [m/(m·Ma)].
0e2	Ksedim			Water sedimentation rate [m/Ma].



Time variables [Ma]:
0	Timeini			Initial time.
10	Timefinal		Final time.
2	tau			Relaxation time (used only for the viscoelastic plate model).
1	dt			Increment time.
10	dtmemounit		Time elapsed between units recording. 
				  if = 0 only file-defined load units will be recorded. 


Boundary Conditions Type:
1	boundary_conds		#0: Left edge is the center of a simmetric model and the plate is not broken there. Right edge is free.
				#1: Broken plate with external force 'appshearforce' and moment 'appmoment' at the left edge. Right edge is free.
				#2: 0 dip and 0 deflection at left and right edges.
				#3: Free edges (0 moment and 0 vertical shear stress).
				#4: Hunging plate with fixed edges and 0 moment.
				#5: Broken plate with external force 'appshearforce' and moment 'appmoment' at the left edge. Right edge is free (zero values).


External forces:
0e12	tecforce		Horizontal tectonic force (compressive if >0).
-1e12	appshearforce		Applied force as bound. cond. in cases 1 and 5. (downwards if <0).
-0e16	appmoment 		Torque as bound. cond. cases 1 and 5. (clockwise if >0).


0	lith_type		To switch the thinplate model of lithosphere:
				#-1: No flexure performance.
				#0: Pure elastic plate model.
				#1: Visco-elastic plate model.
				#2: Elastic-plastic oceanic lithosphere.
				#3: Elastic-plastic continental always decoupled.
				#4: Elastic-plastic continental never decoupled.
				#5: Elastic-plastic continental auto. decoupling.


These are switches to turn on options of the model.
Their possible values are 1 (yes) or 0 (no):
1	switch_sea		For existence of sea.
0	switch_erosed		For erosional-deositional model.
0	grav_anom_type		Gravity anomaly output type. #0: No gravity calculations; #1: Bouguer anomaly;  #2:Free-Air

i/o switches:
1	switch_write_file	For text file output.
1	switch_ps		For postscript output.
0	switch_output		For graphic output.
1	switch_verbose		For more runtime information.
0	switch_debug		For more runtime debugging prints.



(END OF PARAMETERS FILE)

Comments:
    This is a tAo parameter file. 
	--You can modify the format of this parameter files, either by adding 
  more comment lines or changing comments in the existing lines after the 
  values. Comment lines cannot start with a number, this would be read as a 
  parameter. In the first line it must appear the version of tAo.
	--You can run the simplest model (without any load file *.CRG) just 
  varying the b.c. parameters 'appshearforce' & 'appmoment' and the 'tecforce'
  external horizontal force. 
	--Default unities: I.S.  (except indication).
	--If  (switch_topoestable != 0) then the load will rest at zero level 
  and plate subsidence will be filled with 'densinfill' material. Do not use 
  with erosion model.
	--You can get more information about the meaning of each parameter in 
  the tao.h file and tao.info file.

